{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He said</b> — in the manner of prophecy." "<b>Go, love a woman</b> — and take her as a wife, for this is the implication of the word אשה, for he did not mention zonah and the proof is ואכרה לי and afterward she is אוהבת רע, and the meaning is another man, and she commits adultery with him. And the parable is like the one who loves YHWH the children of Israel — that He loved them and they turn to other elohim — this is אהובת רע, and they do not love HaShem but love wine that intoxicates them." "<b>The word אֲשִׁישֵׁי</b> — like סַמְּכוּנִי בָּאֲשִׁישׁוֹת, and the meaning is by the אֲשִׁישׁוֹת of wine, and likewise אֲשִׁישֵׁי יֵין עֲנָבִים. And like it: וְאֲשִׁישָׁה אֶחָת, and there is no need to mention wine."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "Resolved ה' in the phrase אוהב' ה' as referring to YHWH as subject of the love; the construct chain reads 'the one loving YHWH [who loves] the children of Israel,' i.e., YHWH is the lover."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:03.524146512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}